208 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 165 0 R
/E (Operating systems are a primary target for cyber threats such as malware, ransomware, unauthorized access, and network attacks. Operating system hardening is the process of improving system security by applying secure configurations and enabling built-in protection mechanisms to reduce vulnerabilities.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
209 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 165 0 R
/E (This project focuses on the practical hardening and security assessment of a Windows 11 operating system. Various security measures were implemented, including installing Windows security updates, verifying Microsoft Defender Antivirus, reviewing Windows Defender Firewall settings, managing user accounts and privileges, analyzing NTFS file permissions, enabling Controlled Folder Access for ransomware protection, assessing network configuration using PowerShell, reviewing Windows Event Logs, and creating a system restore point.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
210 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 165 0 R
/E (The implementation was carried out using native Windows security tools such as Windows Update, Microsoft Defender, Windows Defender Firewall, Windows PowerShell, Event Viewer, and System Protection. The security posture of the operating system was evaluated before and after applying the hardening measures, and the results were documented with practical observations and screenshots.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
