233 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 167 0 R
/E (An operating system \(OS\) is the core software that manages computer hardware, software resources, and provides essential services for applications. It acts as an interface between users and computer hardware, enabling efficient execution of programs, memory management, file handling, process scheduling, and communication between system components. Popular operating systems include Microsoft Windows, Linux, and macOS, each providing different features and security mechanisms.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
234 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 167 0 R
/E (Operating system hardening is the process of improving the security of an operating system by reducing its attack surface and implementing security best practices. This includes installing security updates, configuring firewall settings, enabling antivirusprotection, restricting user privileges, protecting sensitive files, monitoring system activities, and maintaining reliable backup and recovery mechanisms. A properly hardened operating system is more resistant to cyber threats and unauthorized access. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
235 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 167 0 R
/E (The project provides hands-on experience with practical security controls commonly used in modern Windows environments. It also demonstrates how applying multiple layers of security can significantly improve the overall security posture of an operating system.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
236 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 167 0 R
/T (1.2 Problem Statement)
/E (1.2 Problem Statement)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
237 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 167 0 R
/E (Modern operating systems face numerous security threats due to increasing internet connectivity, software vulnerabilities, and sophisticated cyberattacks. Many users operate their systems with default security settings without understanding the associated risks. Failure to apply security updates, improper user account management, weak access control, disabled security features, and poor monitoring can expose systems to malware, ransomware, and unauthorized access.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
238 0 obj
