522 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 183 0 R
/E (The practical implementation of operating system hardening was successfully completed on a Windows 11 system using built-in Windows security tools and PowerShell. All planned security measures were implemented and verified. The system was evaluated before and after the hardening process to ensure that the security configurations were functioning correctly.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [32]
>>
endobj
523 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 183 0 R
/T (6.2 Discussion)
/E (6.2 Discussion)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [33]
>>
endobj
524 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 183 0 R
/E (The implementation demonstrated that Windows 11 provides several effective built-in security features that can significantly improve system protection when properly configured. Installing the latest security updates reduced exposure to known vulnerabilities, while Microsoft Defender Antivirus provided continuous protection against malware and other malicious software.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [34]
>>
endobj
525 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 184 0 R
/E (The verification of NTFS permissions and the activation of Controlled Folder Access strengthened file security and provided additional protection against ransomware attacks. Network analysis and event log monitoring confirmed that the system was functioning correctly and that security-related activities were being recorded for future analysis.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
526 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 184 0 R
/E (Finally, the creation of a system restore point improved system recoverability by allowing restoration to a previous stable configuration if required.Overall, the practical implementation showed that combining multiple security controls provides a layered defense, making the operating system more resilient against common cyber threats.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
