546 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 185 0 R
/E (This project successfully demonstrated the practical implementation of operating system hardening techniques on a Windows 11 system using built-in Windows security features and PowerShell. The primary objective of enhancing system security through native security mechanisms was achieved by implementing multiple layers of protection.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
547 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 185 0 R
/E (Throughout the project, several security measures were applied, including installing the latest Windows updates, verifying Microsoft Defender Antivirus, reviewing Windows Defender Firewall settings, managing user accounts and privileges,  analyzing NTFS file permissions, enabling Controlled Folder Access, assessing network security, monitoring system logs, and creating a system restore point. Each implementation was verified using Windows administrative tools and PowerShell commands, with observations documented to evaluate their effectiveness.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
548 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 185 0 R
/E (The project demonstrated that a well-configured operating system is significantly more resistant to common cyber threats such as malware, ransomware, unauthorized access, and network-based attacks. It also provided valuable hands-on experience in Windows system administration, cybersecurity best practices, and technical documentation. Overall, this project highlights the importance of regularly maintaining and hardening an operating system to improve its security, reliability, and resilience against evolving cyber threats.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
